<title>SWITZERLAND: Roche's Posicor drug gets Europe approval.</title>
<headline>Roche's Posicor drug gets Europe approval.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roche AG said its Posicor drug for the treatment of high blood pressure and angina had been approved for use in several European countries in line with its approval by the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Belgium, Denmark, Germany, Finland, France, Greece, Britain, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, Austria, Portugal and Spain all admitted the drug in a mutual recognition process linked to the Netherlands' approval, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Authorities in the U.S., Switzerland and several Latin American and Asian countries have also approved the drug.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
